## 2. Target design: slow down at the source, protect at the edge

The idea is to **let Kafka be the buffer** and make the pipeline pull work at the speed the downstream can handle.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    EXT["External app"] -->|"REST, returns 202"| EFA["External facing app"]
    EFA --> K[("Kafka main topic")]
    K -->|"throttled poll"| SUB["Event subscriber, 3 pods<br/>Layer 1: per-pod rate limit<br/>~2.5 tps each"]
    SUB -->|"blocking REST"| ORCH["Domain orchestrator<br/>Layer 2: token bucket 8 tps<br/>per downstream"]
    ORCH --> D1["Downstream API<br/>10 tps"]
    D1 -- "200" --> ORCH
    D1 -. "429 + Retry-After" .-> ORCH
    ORCH -. "429/503 + Retry-After" .-> SUB
    SUB -->|"Layer 3: retry with backoff"| RT[("Retry topic<br/>delayed")]
    RT --> SUB
    RT -->|"max retries exceeded"| DLQ[("Dead letter topic")]

    style SUB fill:#d6f0ff,stroke:#07a
    style ORCH fill:#d6ffd6,stroke:#0a0
    style RT fill:#fff3cd,stroke:#a80
```

